[00:00.00]Alright everyone, let's dive into Lesson 05. Today we're exploring some verbs that are used with the pronouns we and they in English and nos and elas in Portuguese. Now why is this important? Well understanding how to use pronouns and verbs correctly helps us communicate clearly and share our thoughts effectively. On the left, we have English examples. We say things like, we read and they write. These sentences show actions that groups of people do. We write letters every day means a group that includes the speaker is writing letters daily. They like to write poetry means another group enjoys writing poems. On the right, we see that in Portuguese, similar ideas are expressed like this. Nos escrevemos, we write. And elas escrevam, they write. Notice the verb changes slightly to match the pronouns, just like in English. Besides practicing these forms, try to use them in sentences. For instance, nos lemos alguns artigos em inglês translates to, we read some articles in English. Practicing is key. Try saying sentences out loud or writing them down. The more you use these structures, the more natural they'll become. So next time you're talking about what you and your friends enjoy doing, try using we or they with the right verbs. And remember, language learning is all about practice and having fun with it. So keep exploring and using what you've learned today.